  "prefLabel": "Env-Wt 605.02 Additional Requirements for Projects In or Adjacent to Tidal Waters/Wetlands and Tidal Buffer Zones",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wt 605.02 Additional Requirements for Projects In or Adjacent to Tidal Waters/Wetlands and Tidal Buffer Zones. An applicant for a permit for work in or adjacent to tidal waters/wetlands or the tidal buffer zone also shall demonstrate that the following have been avoided or minimized as required by Env-Wt 313.04:\n\n(a) Adverse impacts to beach or tidal flat sediment replenishment;\n\n(b) Adverse impacts to the movement of sediments along a shore;\n\n(c) Adverse impacts on a tidal wetland’s ability to dissipate wave energy and storm surge; and\n\n(d) Adverse impacts of project runoff on salinity levels in tidal environments.\n\nSource. #12806, eff 12-15-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wt600.html"
